# LJ38 index removes the six rigid modes. A curvature is negative only below -max(force_norm, 1e-8*||H||_F, 1e-6).
# Default row. gtol and the iteration budget are the problem force norm and the force-call cap. maxstep is 0.2, the per-atom displacement cap (rgmin atom_maxmove, the same quantity as the eOn max move and the rgmin ASE default). istep is 0.1. BB, DIIS, FIRE, and quickmin take that gradient trial with no line search. L-BFGS, BFGS, CG, steepest descent, Adam, SR1, and SR2 use the session strong Wolfe search, and the first trial is still sized by istep. Newton and dogleg take a Hessian step inside the same cap. Without the cap, an uncapped gradient trial on these starts leaves the Lennard-Jones cutoff. The same values are used for every start.
